---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Src from '../components/Src.astro';
const title = 'How to get an apostille in California';
const description = 'California apostille: the official $20 fee, $6 in-person special handling, Sacramento and Los Angeles offices, mail addresses, and current processing dates from the Secretary of State.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} updated="2026-11-22">
  <h1>How to get an apostille in California</h1>
  <p class="lede">The California Secretary of State issues an apostille that authenticates a California public official’s signature on a document to be used outside the United States. The office issues a single apostille regardless of the destination country; it does not issue a separate authentication certificate.</p>

  <h2>At a glance</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Item</th><th>What the official page says</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Issuing office</td><td>California Secretary of State, Notary Public Section<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/request-apostille" /></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fee by mail</td><td>$20.00 per apostille. Check or money order payable to Secretary of State. The $6 special handling fee does not apply to mail.<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/request-apostille" /></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fee in person</td><td>$20.00 per apostille plus a $6.00 special handling fee for each different public official’s signature being authenticated.<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/apostille-faqs" /></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mail</td><td>Yes, processed only by the Sacramento office, in the order received. Same-day or pulled expedited service is not offered for mail.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mailing addresses</td><td>USPS: Notary Public Section, P.O. Box 942877, Sacramento, CA 94277-0001. FedEx, UPS, DHL, and similar: Notary Public Section, 1500 11th Street, 2nd Floor, Sacramento, CA 95814.<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/request-apostille" /></td></tr>
        <tr><td>In person</td><td>Same-day service at the Sacramento 3rd-floor public counter (1500 11th Street, 3rd Floor, Sacramento, CA 95814) and at the Los Angeles office in the Ronald Reagan building, 300 South Spring Street, Room 12513, Los Angeles, CA 90013 (no appointments). Arrive by 4:30 p.m. to guarantee service.<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/request-apostille" /><Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/processing-times" /></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Processing as published</td><td>In person: typically within 30 minutes after submission. Mail: as of November 20, 2026, Sacramento was processing apostille requests received November 12, 2026.<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/processing-times" /></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What to include</h2>
  <p>Four items are required for a mail request:<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/request-apostille" /></p>
  <ol>
    <li>The document that needs the apostille. It must be signed by a California public official, or be an original notarized and/or certified document. A photocopy is not acceptable.</li>
    <li>A cover sheet stating the country in which the document will be used (the office’s mail cover sheet, or your own).</li>
    <li>A check or money order payable to Secretary of State for $20.00 per apostille.</li>
    <li>A self-addressed envelope for return. Provide prepaid postage if you want a tracked service; otherwise the office returns the document by regular U.S. mail.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Anyone may request an apostille in person, including on behalf of someone else, and the requester does not need to be related to a person named in the document.<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/apostille-faqs" /></p>
  <p>Payment in Sacramento may be by credit card (Visa or Mastercard), check, money order, or cash. The Los Angeles office accepts credit card (Visa or Mastercard), check, or money order; cash is not accepted there.<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/request-apostille" /></p>

  <h2>In-person special handling examples</h2>
  <p>The official FAQ gives these totals for in-person requests, combining the $20 apostille fee with the $6 special handling fee that applies once per distinct public official’s signature:<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/apostille-faqs" /></p>
  <div class="tablewrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Example</th><th>Total</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>1 document, 1 public official</td><td>$26.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2 documents, 1 public official</td><td>$46.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2 documents, 2 public officials</td><td>$52.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>5 documents, 1 public official</td><td>$106.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>5 documents, 5 public officials</td><td>$130.00</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Vital records</h2>
  <p>For California birth and death certificates, the Secretary of State can issue an apostille for the signatures of county clerks and their deputies, county recorders and their deputies, and the State Registrar at the California Department of Public Health. If a city- or county-level certificate is signed by a health officer or county registrar, the official FAQ says you may first need a county-clerk certification or a certified copy from the county recorder or the state Department of Public Health.<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/apostille-faqs" /></p>

  <h2>Office notes when we checked</h2>
  <p>The processing-dates page, last updated November 20, 2026, said the Los Angeles office was temporarily providing services on the 1st floor in suite 1215 because of an elevator outage. Confirm that note on the official page before you go.<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/processing-times" /></p>
  <p>The Secretary of State also holds periodic in-person apostille pop-up shops around the state; dates are listed on the request page.<Src href="https://www.sos.ca.gov/notary/request-apostille" /></p>

